<http://data.silknow.org/object/0f3fafed-513b-3368-892f-6a2ec44f0625>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Iron mask, hammered from behind (repousse); throat-guard of lacquered plates laced with silk; patterned silk and leather attachment"@en , "This mask forms part of a Japanese suit of armour and is made of iron.  It has been hammered from behind using the repousse technique.  The throat-guard is of lacquered plates laced with silk and it has a patterned silk and leather attachment. \n\nThe mask went on display at an exhibition entitled 'Japanese Lacquer and Metalwork', held at the Burlington Fine Arts Club in 1894."@en , "Iron mask, hammered from behind (repousse); throat-guard of lacquered plates laced with silk; patterned silk and leather attachment, Japan, ca. 1700-1850"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1e18e921-c64d-3b12-8cdf-5c8bbf60983f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/81345747-83ea-3ed7-93b0-20b98a96c615> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Iron mask, hammered from behind (repousse); throat-guard of lacquered plates laced with silk; patterned silk and leather attachment"@en , "Iron mask, hammered from behind (repousse); throat-guard of lacquered plates laced with silk; patterned silk and leather attachment, Japan, ca. 1700-1850"@en , "This mask forms part of a Japanese suit of armour and is made of iron.  It has been hammered from behind using the repousse technique.  The throat-guard is of lacquered plates laced with silk and it has a patterned silk and leather attachment. \n\nThe mask went on display at an exhibition entitled 'Japanese Lacquer and Metalwork', held at the Burlington Fine Arts Club in 1894."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "M.52:4-1909" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O199649> .

